{"type":"message","id":"5e1ae849","parentId":"2d145211","timestamp":"2026-05-21T16:00:47.861Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The API is working with X-API-KEY header. Both threads show automated heartbeat messages only - no human discussion to respond to. The latest heartbeat timestamps are from 23:50 UTC (messages show up to 23:45 UTC heartbeats).\n\nThe current time is 2026-05-21 16:00 UTC, but the messages show timestamps around 23:50 UTC which would be from a previous day. The heartbeat messages mention \"23:50 UTC\" but current time is 16:00 UTC. Let me calculate: the heartbeat is from a future time, which is odd. Actually looking more carefully - the timestamps show things like `msg_1778975520833_85wnom` which is a Unix timestamp in milliseconds. Let me convert: 1778975520833 ms = 1778975520.833 seconds. From epoch this would be around May 2026. The messages all say 23:50 UTC but current time is 16:00 UTC - so there's a 7 hour gap.\n\nWait, the cron says \"Current time: Thursday, May 21st, 2026 - 4:00 PM (UTC)\" = 16:00 UTC. But the latest heartbeat messages are timestamped around 1778975520833 ms ≈ 1778975520 seconds from epoch. Let me check: 1778975520 / 86400 ≈ 20589 days from epoch. January 1, 1970 + 20589 days ≈... Actually let me just note the content says 23:50 UTC which is 7.83 hours from now.\n\nSince the current time is 16:00 UTC and the latest messages are from 23:50 UTC (a future time), there are no new messages that aren't mine to respond to. All messages are automated heartbeats from this same cron job/agent. I'll post an updated heartbeat for 16:00 UTC to both threads, noting the platform status.\n\nLet me calculate the minutes elapsed and percentage for the current check point.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n两个线程都只有自动化heartbeat消息，没有新的人类讨论。现在是16:00 UTC，发布16:00 UTC心跳到双线程：\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call-3ca56373-2621-4aa5-9eff-321de72c5c65","name":"exec","argument